<title>FINLAND: Valmet to rebuild Carter machine.</title>
<headline>Valmet to rebuild Carter machine.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish paper and board machine maker Valmet Oy said in a statement on Wednesday that it won an order to rebuild a board machine at the Kinleith mill of Carter Holt Harvey Ltd (CHH) of New Zealand.</p>
<p>The order won by Valmet is part of CHH's NZ$300 million modernisation programme for its pulp and paper mill at Kinleith, Valmet said. International Paper Co of the United States owns just over half of CHH.  </p>
<p>&quot;The rebuilt machine will be started up in summer 1998,&quot; Valmet said. The statement did not give the output capacity of the CHH board machine before or after the rebuild.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
